{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZfNo8cst9yxoynpHuPS8R","type":"tool_result","content":"=== tech-design: deviation table + E02-NB-001 + DD-4 ===\n79:**DD-4: The scheduler is an SDK-internal module, not a domain and not part of the queue util.** `tech-utils/work-queue` stays storage-only (it gains claim/complete functions, still pure SQL against an open handle). The scheduler — per-thread single-flight flag, pending-coalesce flag, post-commit pokes, mode selection — lives in `src/scheduler.ts` at the SDK assembly layer, because it is the one component that holds cross-operation in-memory state and constructs its own short-lived `OperationContext`s outside any caller transaction. Hosts never see it; they see `mode: \"background\" | \"manual\"` at SDK construction.\n485:### Deviation Table\n489:| — | (none at design time; implementation-time deviations land here) | | | |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9c65f8a-2769-45ee-8250-eab6f8fa0e38","uuid":"b0533a38-31cc-4f58-bd8c-7b7d98d6df27","timestamp":"2026-06-11T10:00:35.966Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== tech-design: deviation table + E02-NB-001 + DD-4 ===\n79:**DD-4: The scheduler is an SDK-internal module, not a domain and not part of the queue util.** `tech-utils/work-queue` stays storage-only (it gains claim/complete functions, still pure SQL against an open handle). The scheduler — per-thread single-flight flag, pending-coalesce flag, post-commit pokes, mode selection — lives in `src/scheduler.ts` at the SDK assembly layer, because it is the one component that holds cross-operation in-memory state and constructs its own short-lived `OperationContext`s outside any caller transaction. Hosts never see it; they see `mode: \"background\" | \"manual\"` at SDK construction.\n485:### Deviation Table\n489:| — | (none at design time; implementation-time deviations land here) | | | |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":fa