{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011kamopEdmSDwi2qGEx8ppr","type":"tool_result","content":"478\t| 5 Edit | mutation validation, cascade module, source-version check, supersede | TC-5.4 stale-result check (scripted double: claim before edit, complete after) |\n479\t| 6 Delete | deleted_at stamps, filtered reads everywhere, initiating-prompt refusal, turn delete, empty chunk | TC-6.1 events-survive-delete; TC-6.5 bounded cascade; TC-6.7 triple-refusal |\n480\t\n481\tDependencies are strictly linear (each chunk's tests use the previous chunk's machinery). Chunk 1 is the long pole; its process-suite tests are the epic's hardest fixtures and get designed first in the test plan.\n482\t\n483\tVerification gates: unchanged scripts. New tests slot into the existing suites: `work-execution.test.ts`, `derivation-messages.test.ts`, `derivation-turns.test.ts`, `report-repair.test.ts`, `mutations.test.ts`, `cli-process-work.test.ts`, plus fixture additions. The test plan maps every TC to its file with setup and assertion.\n484\t\n485\t### Deviation Table\n486\t\n487\t| # | Deviates from | What | Why | Status |\n488\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n489\t| — | (none at design time; implementation-time deviations land here) | | | |\n490\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9c65f8a-2769-45ee-8250-eab6f8fa0e38","uuid":"9202d788-29c9-483d-8b86-078aa7b34200","timestamp":"2026-06-11T10:00:38.786Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md","content":"| 5 Edit | mutation validation, cascade module, source-version check, supersede | TC-5.4 stale-result check (scripted double: claim before edit, complete after) |\n| 6 Delete | deleted_at stamps, filtered reads everywhere, initiating-prompt refusal, turn delete, empty chunk | TC-6.1 events-survive-delete; TC-6.5 bounded cascade; TC-6.7 triple-refusal |\n\nDependencies are strictly linear (each chunk's tests use the previous chunk's machinery). Chunk 1 is the long pole; its process-suite tests are the epic's hardest fixtures and get designed first in the test plan.\n\nVerification gates: unchanged scripts. New tests slot into the existing suites: `work-execution.test.ts`, `derivation-messages.test.ts`, `derivation-turns.test.ts`, `report-repair.test.ts`, `mutations.test.ts`, `cli-process-work.test.ts`, plus fixture additions. The test plan maps every TC to its file with setup and assertion.\n\n### Deviation Table\n\n| # | Deviates from | What | Why | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| — | (none at design time; implementation-time deviations land here) | | | |\n","numLines":13,"startLine":478,"totalLines":490}}}
