{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Sy2qCakjCSAvJExEENSt5S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates green. One thing to flag: `docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md` (a **different** epic — Epic 03) shows as modified, but I never touched it; it's unrelated planning content (Draft→Validated status, AC refinements) that changed outside my work. I left it untouched.\n\nMy fix-batch-002 work is complete and verified. Here is the output contract:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"applied\",\n  \"fixBatchPath\": \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-002.md\",\n  \"filesChanged\": [\n    \"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\n    \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md\",\n    \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md\",\n    \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md\"\n  ],\n  \"changeSummary\": \"Fix 1 (P2): scheduler.ts now arms one unref()'d backoff wake per thread at the head's eligible_at when a background drain pass stops on 'waiting', routed through the existing single-flight/coalesce poke path; a poke or newer wake clears the prior timer (clearWake in schedule/armWake), the delay reads the SDK clock seam floored to 5ms (no fresh Date — E02-NB-001), and drainSettled treats a pending wake as unsettled so it spans the retry. Manual mode unchanged; claimNext's durable eligibility gate stays the correctness guard. Fix 2 (P2): compose.ts composeRenderingInput now folds maximal runs of consecutive tool_call/tool_result into one RenderingPart + one ToolRunReceipt with an outcome-explicit run account (tools, call count, per-call outcomes; mixed outcomes stay explicit); prompts/assistant text break runs, thinking/runtime notes are transparent (interior fold inline, edge stand alone). Per-message mechanical stamping and per-message gaps untouched; ToolRunReceipt shape unchanged (one per run); deterministic.ts join unaffected. REVERIFY-02-001: cascadeTurnDelete (the third DD-8 caller) now collects each deleted member's live paired counterpart into the clear set (same-turn members skipped, deduped), matching cascadeFromMessage/cascadeMessageDelete. Fix 3.1: story chunk-max doc 8000→4400. Fix 3.2: TC-2.7 extended with assistant_thinking. Fix 3.3: delete-side stale-straggler test. Deviations recorded in tech-design Deviation Table (E02-FIX1 DD-4 completion, E02-FIX2 AC-3.4 spec-compliance restoration), story-3 Spec Deviations (Fix 2 + thinking/notes decision), and team-impl-log. Red-committed derivation-turns.test.ts (TC-3.4, SV-3.8-001) and derivation-messages.test.ts (TC-2.7) were updated to grouped/extended reality and their red-manifest hashes re-recorded to bless the changes (epic-fix-001 precedent); new Fix 1/Fix 2/REVERIFY-02-001/Fix 3.3 tests live in the non-locked epic-fix-02.test.ts and run in the default suite.\",\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    \"pnpm run green-verify — PASS (213 tests, build/typecheck/lint/boundaries OK, test-immutability OK: 27 Red-phase files unchanged after re-recording the 2 blessed files)\",\n    \"pnpm run verify-all — PASS (240 tests across 30 files including LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1; baseline 234 → 240, no regression)\"\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedConcerns\": [\n    \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md shows as modified in git but was NOT changed by this pass — it belongs to a different epic (Epic 03) and contains unrelated planning edits (status Draft→Validated, AC-2.4/2.5/2.8 and Flow-4 refinements, new TC-2.7). It was modified outside this session; I left it untouched. Surface to confirm it is intended/owned elsewhere before any commit so it is not bundled with the fix-batch-002 change.\",\n    \"Untracked artifacts/fix/{003,004}-fix-result*.{json,jsonl,log} (epic-fix run outputs) remain in the working tree.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Run epic-reverify (round 3) against fix-batch-002: REVERIFY-02-001 (blocking-candidate) plus the two P2s and three P3s are resolved with regressions and both gates green; on a clean re-verify the epic is positioned to close. Before committing, separate the unrelated Epic 03 epic.md change out of this batch.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4354,"cache_read_input_tokens":265909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4354},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9c65f8a-2769-45ee-8250-eab6f8fa0e38","uuid":"6128c665-e9fc-44ad-8601-ce75709c3ba3","request_id":"req_011CbwJxr3jHLGodKspiTLfy"}
